---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import HomeownerForm from "../components/HomeownerForm.astro";
---
<Base title="me | ghost-watts" pathname="/me">
  <section class="max-w-prose mx-auto px-6 pt-8 pb-2">
    <h1 class="text-3xl mb-3">Estimate your roof</h1>
    <p class="text-ink-700 leading-relaxed">
      Drop your address, your roof area, and your monthly Meralco bill. We compute solar potential at your lat/lon using the European Commission's PVGIS API (free, no auth, no signup), look up your city's signal strength from the latest ghost-watts release, and pull your LGU's permit fee from the hand-curated friction table. All math is client-side. Nothing about you is sent anywhere except OpenStreetMap (geocoding) and PVGIS (solar irradiance), both of which are free public services.
    </p>
  </section>

  <HomeownerForm />

  <section class="max-w-prose mx-auto px-6 py-6 text-xs text-ink-500">
    Estimates only. Not engineering advice. Talk to a certified installer before committing.
  </section>
</Base>
